# Plan diagrams

When you write or update a plan in Plan mode, or edit a `.plan.md` file, put one mermaid diagram near the top, before the long explanation and before code.

The diagram is the big picture. A reader should see who talks to whom and what changes, without reading the prose.

- One diagram. Add a second only when the first cannot show a separate flow.
- Use words a person would say. Leave out function signatures, flag lists, and file paths.
- Prefer `flowchart` with a few nodes. Label edges with the action.
- Keep the written plan. The diagram does not replace the steps.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  person[You] --> app[Opero]
  app --> browser[Browser]
  browser --> site[Website]
  site -->|page| app
```
